    "updated_at": "2025-10-10T07:14:31Z",
    "body": "The [update-the-image-data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#update-the-image-data) will do it if it will be invoked, but there are two conditions to trigger it\n\n1. **4.8.4.3.1 When to obtain images** ([when-to-obtain-images](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#when-to-obtain-images))\n\nIt is mostly about on-demand image loading (bandwidth-constrained network?!), but it has some sentence to do sync update the image data for newly created element, but per my understanding it is not 100% fulfill this test case, otherwise it will make slight overhead on each element creation (by running microtask to change current request's state from `unavailable` to `broken` with empty `src` and `srcset` attributes?!).\n\n`When obtaining images immediately, the user agent must synchronously update the image data of the img element, with the restart animation flag set if so stated, whenever that element is created or has experienced relevant mutations.`\n\n2. **4.8.4.3.2 Reacting to DOM mutations** ([reacting-to-dom-mutations](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#reacting-to-dom-mutations))\nNone of mentioned conditions for experienced relevant mutations cover this test case.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
