    "created_at": "2025-10-10T09:41:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-10T09:41:09Z",
    "body": "Ok, in summary the specification require to obtain image immediately (by default) on the 'img` element creation (eg. by calling [update-the-image-data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#update-the-image-data) on legacy Image contructor ([step 2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-image))\n\nBut it is up to UA implementation how to handle it with minimal overhead:\n- Chromium/Firefox use `nullable` current request to handle it (like unspecified `None` state for [current request](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#img-req-state))\n- Servo use non-spec state validation in certain conditions (`decode` step 2) ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
